{"title":"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Simple_logic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Simple logic)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#What&#39;s_happening_here?_Why_isn&#39;t_the_answer_&quot;B&quot;_?\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">What's happening here? Why isn't the answer \"B\"&#160;?</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> men working <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> hours a day for each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> days produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> articles, then the number of articles \n(not necessarily an integer) produced by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> men working <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> hours a day for each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> days is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee5dbe475d059cde325143cc42fbab0647f3578.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{x^3}{y^2}\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{y^3}{x^2}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{x^2}{y^3}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{y^2}{x^3}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"400\" height=\"42\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of articles produced per hour per person.  By using dimensional analysis,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/0/7e0ec763293e49ef6b992c7e08bda9060124e511.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{x \\text{ hours}}{\\text{day}} \\cdot x \\text{ days} \\cdot \\frac{k \\text{ articles}}{\\text{hours} \\cdot \\text{person}} \\cdot x \\text{ people} = x \\text{ articles}\\]\" width=\"404\" height=\"40\" />\nSolving this yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/6/3f6a0ff1ba678e1ec404730bfb414de61fd79229.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = \\frac{1}{x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />.  Using dimensional analysis again, the number of articles produced by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> men working <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> hours a day for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> days is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/3/ac3b76ca978d08d0ca2f69cbf0754b07117e5779.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{y \\text{ hours}}{\\text{day}} \\cdot y \\text{ days} \\cdot \\frac{\\frac{1}{x^2} \\text{ articles}}{\\text{hours} \\cdot \\text{person}} \\cdot y \\text{ people} = \\frac{y^3}{x^2} \\text{ articles}\\]\" width=\"413\" height=\"44\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Simple_logic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Simple_logic)\">Solution 2 (Simple logic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Simple logic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The question is based on the assumption that each person, each hour, each day, will be produce a constant number of items (maybe fractional).\n</p><p>So it takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> men <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> hours to produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da1d41e79c2e0e357c7c8bdd93ec2d0e879f2fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{x}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"46\" height=\"33\" /> item in a day.\n</p><p>In a similar manner, 1 man, 1 hour, for a day, can produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a84a13e3fc6963417df14ae3af524f14e4b53fd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" /> items. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> men, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> hours a day, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> days produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce7a59e9f10788d6540463b0ec795af94e11ec0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y^3}{x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"41\" /> items. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>Dimensional analysis is definitely the most rigid, but if you know the ending units (e.g. you know that density is measured in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/4/af4b2f94adcfc69b713518f78d028b78ddfa1ccb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g/cm^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"21\" /> or something like that, you can just treat is as simple proportions and equations.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>By Ajeet Dubey | <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://ioqm.in\">ioqm.in</a></i>\n</p><p>The first situation uses\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd73654d0def2d321c4095f966cf840db67de695.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\cdot x\\cdot x=x^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"17\" />\nman-hours and produces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> articles. Therefore the production rate is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4efc1c1121fb523d496e9ed1ea5107156ce1b05a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{x^3}=\\frac1{x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"38\" />\narticle per man-hour.\n</p><p>In the second situation there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c59beae24503129ca7d331ce1116da501038e30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y\\cdot y\\cdot y=y^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> man-hours. Hence the number of articles produced is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/e/8fe1d0238f7716729c507b4010d59733e3c5d784.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^3\\cdot\\frac1{x^2}=\\frac{y^3}{x^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"105\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/1/a2194b81820e8380be586c1564c3f5d03d5c100d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"42\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"What.27s_happening_here.3F_Why_isn.27t_the_answer_.22B.22_.3F\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"What's_happening_here?_Why_isn't_the_answer_&quot;B&quot;_?\">What's happening here? Why isn't the answer \"B\"&#160;?</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: What&#39;s happening here? Why isn&#39;t the answer &quot;B&quot;&#160;?\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that if we change the problem to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> men produce <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> items a day, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> men produces how many items a day, then the answer would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. In this case, it would be a direct variation. However, notice that direct variations only have two factors --- an independent and dependent variable each (cause-effect, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />). However, there are 3 factors, not 1, that are contributing to how many items are produced in the original problem. This is a joint variation problem, not a direct variation problem. This is the reason why the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" /> (also see that the base unit (1 man/1 hour/1 day) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/4/a84a13e3fc6963417df14ae3af524f14e4b53fd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{x^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"24\" height=\"38\" />).\n</p><p>Hope that solves your confusions.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME\" title=\"1961 AHSME\">1961 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1961 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1961\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> 